* Checkpoint 3 (v2): ARBNO and BAL, the two Movement III primitives
* this checkpoint originally shipped without -- see PROCESS.md and
* interpreter/README.md's scope decisions for the disclosed fix.
* research/snobol/03-pattern-matching.md: `ARBNO(p) = NULL | p
* *ARBNO(p)`, and BAL is built from NOTANY + ARBNO, not a hand-written
* paren-depth counter.
* ARBNO(ANY(s)): grows shortest-first through a run of digits, only as
* far as needed for what follows (here, up to the trailing '.').
        S1 = '3.14159'
        S1 ARBNO(ANY('0123456789')) . INTPART '.'   :F(BADARBNO)
        OUTPUT = 'ARBNO CAPTURED INTPART=' INTPART
* BAL: the shortest nonnull balanced-parenthesis run, bound with "."
* just like any other pattern -- confirming BAL is a real composed
* pattern value, not special-cased plumbing.
        S2 = '(A(B)C)DE)'
        S2 BAL . GROUP                              :F(BADBAL)
        OUTPUT = 'BAL CAPTURED GROUP=' GROUP        :(END)
BADARBNO  OUTPUT = 'UNREACHABLE (ARBNO)'
BADBAL    OUTPUT = 'UNREACHABLE (BAL)'
END       N = N
